From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 23:35:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: qcom: matisse3g: describe standalone CPU collapse

The upstream MSM8226 SPM driver already contains the CPU standalone
power-collapse sequence used by SM-T531. Connect its existing CPUidle
driver to the four cores. The stock DT specifies 500 us latency and a
broadcast timer for standalone collapse. Use a conservative 2 ms minimum
residency, above the stock 1200 us time overhead.

This keeps the L2 cache powered and does not implement system-wide RPM
sleep or L2 power collapse.

Signed-off-by: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g.dts
index 44ba2dc07..ac38f3d67 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/qcom/qcom-msm8226-samsung-matisse3g.dts
@@ -392,3 +392,32 @@ opp-1190400000 {
 		opp-microvolt = <1280000>;
 	};
 };
+
+/ {
+	cpus {
+		idle-states {
+			cpu_spc: cpu-spc {
+				compatible = "qcom,idle-state-spc", "arm,idle-state";
+				wakeup-latency-us = <500>;
+				min-residency-us = <2000>;
+				local-timer-stop;
+			};
+		};
+	};
+};
+
+&cpu0 {
+	cpu-idle-states = <&cpu_spc>;
+};
+
+&cpu1 {
+	cpu-idle-states = <&cpu_spc>;
+};
+
+&cpu2 {
+	cpu-idle-states = <&cpu_spc>;
+};
+
+&cpu3 {
+	cpu-idle-states = <&cpu_spc>;
+};
